.Dd April 22, 2026
.Dt HOST_TOOLCHAIN 7
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm host_toolchain
.Nd building, installing, and using the Substrate host toolchain
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The Substrate repository can build host-runnable copies of its toolchain and
selected userland utilities for validation on a Linux host.
The staged output lives in
.Pa host_dist/
and can be synchronized into an install prefix such as
.Pa /opt/substrate .
.Sh BUILDING
Build the staged host tool tree with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make host_dist
.Ed
.Pp
By default,
.Dq Li host_dist
uses the system host compiler for native rebuilds
.Pq typically Pa /usr/bin/cc
so rebuilding the installed toolchain does not recursively invoke the
Substrate
.Xr cc 1
driver unless
.Ev HOSTCC
is set explicitly.
.Sh INSTALLING
Install the staged host tree into
.Pa /opt/substrate
with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo make HOST_DIST_PREFIX=/opt/substrate host_install
.Ed
.Pp
The install step rebuilds
.Pa host_dist/
and then synchronizes its contents into the chosen prefix.
.Ev HOST_DIST_PREFIX
may be used to select a different install location.
.Sh USING THE INSTALLED TOOLCHAIN
To prefer the installed Substrate tools for host-native validation, place the
installed directories first in
.Ev PATH :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
export PATH=/opt/substrate/usr/bin:/opt/substrate/bin:$PATH
.Ed
.Pp
After that,
.Xr cc 1
will resolve the sibling installed
.Xr as 1
and
.Xr ld 1
from the same prefix before falling back to other tools on
.Ev PATH .
Use
.Dq Li cc -###
to print the exact assembler and linker commands that will be used.
.Pp
To force exact backend paths in mixed environments:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
AS=/opt/substrate/usr/bin/as LD=/opt/substrate/usr/bin/ld cc -m64 hello.c -o hello64
.Ed
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width HOST_DIST_PREFIX
.It Ev HOSTCC
Override the compiler used to rebuild host-native tools during
.Dq Li make host_dist
and
.Dq Li make host_install .
.It Ev HOST_DIST_PREFIX
Select the installation prefix used by
.Dq Li make host_install .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa host_dist/
Staged host-runnable toolchain and utility tree.
.It Pa /opt/substrate/usr/bin/cc
Installed host compiler driver when the default prefix is used.
.It Pa /opt/substrate/usr/bin/as
Installed host assembler when the default prefix is used.
.It Pa /opt/substrate/usr/bin/ld
Installed host linker when the default prefix is used.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr as 1 ,
.Xr cc 1 ,
.Xr ld 1